**Status**: Draft — three decisions ruled (host-or-VM binding, challenge-match dropped, score device-internal and the threshold that falls out of it), two open and device-internal (failure raised-or-returned, threshold-in-series). A fourth invariant is now RATIFIED (2026-08-24): [CXC-FPHAL-MATCH-USES-ENROLL-SENSOR], the fail-loud-plus-live-rebind fix for the mock/real-sensor fork closed by [DEC-R503-UX-HAL-LIVE-REBIND-FIX]; the GRANTED end-to-end run that proved it live is recorded at [CXC-R503-AURALED]'s evidence slot in C70. [CXC-FPHAL-MOCK-ROLE] now carries the ratified use-envelope (X/Y/Z legitimate uses, gated by FP_ALLOW_MOCK where applicable, and the NEVER-silent-production-fallback rule) plus the structural build-time guard, per [DEC-R503-MOCK-STRUCTURAL-GUARD] — David chose annotate-AND-guard over annotate-only. No mock and no parity test exist yet as landed code in THIS spec corpus's own tracking; the live e2e ran on the built firmware described in C70/C73, not against an artifact this document names.
